        title: 'Best Time for Wildlife Viewing at Borana Conservancy',
        description: `The best time to visit Borana Conservancy for wildlife viewing is during the dry seasons of June to October and January to February. During these periods, wildlife is most concentrated around water sources, vegetation is lower improving visibility, and rhino tracking conditions are at their safest and most productive. African wild dogs can be encountered year-round and are often denning with pups between February and May, making the wet season an excellent time for wild dog enthusiasts. Borana's resident wildlife and expert guiding ensure rewarding game drives in every month of the year.`
