      highlights: {
        title: 'Wildlife Highlights — Samburu Special Five & Northern Kenya Safari',
        description: `Buffalo Springs National Reserve is the definitive home of the "Samburu Special Five" — five northern-adapted species found in very few other places on Earth. The reticulated giraffe, with its bold geometric patterning, is the most beautiful of Africa's giraffes. Grevy's zebra, the world's largest and most endangered wild zebra, mingles with the equally striking Beisa oryx. The gerenuk — "the giraffe-necked antelope" — feeds standing upright on its hind legs to reach high browse. The Somali ostrich, with its distinctive blue-grey neck, completes the five. Alongside these iconic species, the Ewaso Nyiro River sustains enormous elephant herds, resident leopards frequently seen in riverine figs, and lion prides that hunt along the water's edge. Nile crocodiles lurk in the deeper pools, and the buffalo springs themselves form a year-round wildlife focal point.`
      },
