        title: 'Best Time for Wildlife Viewing in Buffalo Springs',
        description: `The best time to visit Buffalo Springs National Reserve is during the dry season from June to October and the short dry period of January to February. During these months, wildlife concentrates predictably along the Ewaso Nyiro River and at the buffalo springs, making sightings dense and reliable. All five Samburu Special Five are present year-round, but the open vegetation in the dry season makes locating gerenuk, oryx, and Grevy's zebra in the inland scrublands significantly easier. Big-cat activity is highest during the cooler early mornings and late afternoons throughout the year.`
