        description: `Buffalo Springs is an excellent birding destination year-round, but the best birding season is from November to April when Palearctic and intra-African migrants arrive, dramatically boosting species counts. The Ewaso Nyiro River corridor is productive throughout the year for waterbirds, kingfishers, and African fish eagle. The dry season months of June to October offer the best conditions for locating arid-zone specialists and raptors, with vegetation thinned and species more active in the early morning cool.`
