        description: `Hell's Gate is an excellent raptor-watching destination year-round, but soaring activity is best during the warm midday hours when thermal columns build above the volcanic cliffs. Lammergeier and Verreaux's eagle are present year-round as resident nesters. October to April sees additional migratory species. Morning visits (6–11am) are best for songbirds and active species, while mid-morning to early afternoon is best for soaring raptor observation above the gorge walls.`
