      introText: `Hell's Gate National Park can be enjoyed year-round, but the ideal visiting window is the dry season from June to October and January to February. Dry conditions make cycling, gorge walking, and rock climbing most comfortable and safe, and the clear Rift Valley air is perfect for raptor watching. The park is extremely accessible from Nairobi and works equally well as a day trip or overnight stop combined with Lake Naivasha. Avoid weekends and public holidays if possible — weekday visits are significantly more peaceful.`,
