        title: 'Wildlife Highlights — Lions, Elephants & the Tana River Wilderness',
        description: `Kora National Park is inseparable from the story of George Adamson and his life's work rehabilitating lions in this eastern Kenya wilderness. Today, Kora's lions — protected and studied for over 50 years — represent one of Kenya's most significant lion populations outside the major parks. Large elephant herds use the Tana River corridor as a movement route between Meru, Kora, and the wider eastern Kenya ecosystem. Leopards are regularly encountered on and around the dramatic granite kopjes, using the elevated rock faces as observation points and kill storage sites. The Tana River itself supports hippos, Nile crocodiles, and a remarkable concentration of waterbirds including African fish eagle, goliath heron, and African skimmer.`
