        title: 'Best Time for Wildlife Viewing in Kora National Park',
        description: `The best time to visit Kora National Park is during the dry seasons of June to October and January to February. During dry periods, wildlife concentrates predictably along the Tana River and the permanent water sources within the park, making sightings of lions, elephants, and hippos more reliable. The dramatically reduced vegetation in the dry season also improves visibility across the thorn-scrub habitats. A fly-in visit is strongly recommended year-round for access, but the dry season makes road access from Meru significantly more feasible for those with appropriate vehicles.`
