        description: `Laikipia is excellent for birdwatching year-round, with the richest diversity from November to April when Palearctic migrants swell the species count. The dry season (June–October) is particularly good for raptors, with Verreaux's eagle and martial eagle active on the rocky scarps. Jackson\'s widowbird — a Kenyan endemic — displays in highland grasslands near the plateau escarpments from April to August. Walking safaris focused on birdwatching are available at several Laikipia conservancies year-round.`
