        title: 'Wildlife Highlights — Rhino, Leopard & the Lake Nakuru Big Five',
        description: `Lake Nakuru National Park is Kenya's benchmark for reliable rhino viewing — both black and white rhino are frequently encountered on morning game drives, making this one of the few places in East Africa where guests can almost guarantee seeing rhino on a two-day visit. The park's leopard population is among the most accessible in Kenya, with the resident cats regularly found in the yellow fever acacia woodland on the lake's western shore. Rothschild's giraffe — a critically endangered subspecies with fewer than 3,000 individuals remaining globally — reach their highest density in any Kenyan national park here, and are commonly seen posing against the lake backdrop for photographers. Lion prides control the highland grasslands, and the resident hippo pods occupy the lake shore year-round.`
