        description: `Lake Nakuru is outstanding for birdwatching year-round with over 450 recorded species. The flamingo spectacle — when present in good numbers — is most reliable from October to March. Palearctic migrants arrive from November and boost species counts significantly. The yellow fever woodland is exceptional for forest birds including numerous sunbird species, warblers, and resident raptors. The Baboon Cliff area and the highland forest on the escarpment provide access to high-altitude species not found on the lake shore.`
