          excerpt: 'Standing at the Koobi Fora fossil beds, holding a cast of a 1.6-million-year-old Homo erectus skull found metres from where you stand — that experience redefines what a destination means. The jade lake, the volcanic desert, the enormous sky — Lake Turkana is unlike anywhere else on Earth.',
          fullReview: 'Standing at the Koobi Fora fossil beds, holding a cast of a 1.6-million-year-old Homo erectus skull found metres from where you stand — that is an experience that redefines what a destination means. The jade lake behind you, the volcanic desert all around, the sky enormous above — Lake Turkana is unlike anywhere else on Earth. The crocodile spectacle on Central Island, the El Molo fishermen, the Dassanach ceremonies — this is a landscape of extraordinary depth and meaning that every serious Africa traveller should experience at least once.',
