        title: 'Wildlife Highlights — Elephants, Wild Dogs & the Laikipia Landscape',
        description: `Loisaba's most celebrated wildlife spectacle is its elephant population — large multigenerational herds that move through the conservancy's 56,000 acres and gather at the permanent Ewaso Nyiro River and waterhole system, providing some of the most intimate and reliable elephant viewing in Laikipia. African wild dogs have established resident packs at Loisaba; the pack hunting behaviour across the open plateau grasslands is among the most thrilling wildlife encounters in northern Kenya. Grevy's zebra — the world's most endangered wild equid — are present in significant numbers throughout the conservancy. Lion prides, resident leopards, cheetah, stripped hyena, caracal, and the full complement of Laikipia ungulates — including Beisa oryx, reticulated giraffe, Günther's dik-dik, and gerenuk — complete a northern Kenya wildlife community of exceptional richness.`
