          fullReview: 'I have spent eighteen years in the Masai Mara ecosystem. Naboisho is where I bring every visitor who wants to understand what the Mara truly is — before it became congested with vehicles and tourist pressure. The lion density is extraordinary: multiple prides with dozens of individuals, from tiny cubs to giant-maned males in their absolute prime. The walking safari across the Naboisho plains with no other human in sight is one of the most profound wildlife experiences Kenya offers. Combined with the night drive capability and the off-road access that simply doesn\'t exist in the national reserve, Naboisho delivers the Mara at its most elemental.',
