          park: 'US', parkFlag: 'us',
          title: 'Seven lions at breakfast. Not a single other vehicle. I wept.',
          rating: 5, date: 'August 8, 2025',
          excerpt: 'Seven lions eating a zebra kill at 7am. We were ten metres away for 45 minutes. No other vehicle. No radio calls. Just seven lions and us and the Mara morning.',
          fullReview: 'We had seven lions — a pride of five with two large males — eating a fresh zebra kill at 7am on our second morning. We were parked ten metres away in total silence for 45 minutes. At one point the dominant male raised his head and looked directly at me. Not at the vehicle — at me. No other vehicle came. No radio calls brought anyone else to the sighting. Just seven lions, the sound of bone and sinew, and the Mara morning stretching to the horizon. I have never experienced anything like it. I wept on the way back to camp. I am not ashamed.',
