      highlights: {
        title: 'Wildlife Highlights — Lions, Cheetahs & the Exclusive Mara',
        description: `Mara Naboisho Conservancy holds the highest density of lions of any protected area recorded globally — multiple large prides with territories across the conservancy's 50,000 acres, producing sightings of a frequency and intimacy that simply cannot be replicated in the national reserve. Resident cheetah coalitions (including the famous area coalitions of three to five male cheetahs) and females with cubs are encountered regularly throughout the open conservancy grasslands. Leopard are reliably present in the riparian forest corridors and rocky terrain. Elephant bulls and family groups move through the conservancy year-round. During the Wildebeest Migration season from July to October, enormous herds spill into the conservancy from the national reserve, drawing additional lion activity and providing extraordinary concentrations of prey. Hyena clans, jackal, bat-eared fox, serval, and aardvark complete a predator community of exceptional diversity.`
      },
