        description: `Marsabit is most productive for birdwatching from October to April when Palearctic migrants supplement the resident species and the crater lakes attract their greatest waterbird diversity. The montane forest is excellent year-round for forest species — African crowned eagle, Hemprich's hornbill, Narina trogon, and African emerald cuckoo are all resident. The highland forest edge is the best place for the near-endemic brown-tailed rock chat and hunter's cisticola. A specialist birding guide based in Marsabit town is strongly recommended for serious birding visits.`
