          excerpt: 'Two thousand wildebeest entered the river at once. The sound — the bellowing, the water, the crocodiles — was something I will hear in my sleep for the rest of my life. I had seen this on television a hundred times. Nothing — absolutely nothing — prepares you for it in person.'
