      wildlifePreview: {
        description: 'The Masai Mara supports one of the greatest concentrations of large mammals on Earth across its 1,510km² of savannah and riverine habitat. The reserve is defined by its extraordinary lion population — multiple large, well-studied prides including the BBC-famous Marsh Pride — alongside resident cheetah, leopard, elephant, buffalo, hippo, and the seasonal Wildebeest Migration that brings 1.5 million animals north from July to October.',
        linkText: 'More about the wildlife'
      },

      thingsToDoPreview: [
        {
          description: 'Morning and evening game drives across the Mara plains, sunrise hot air balloon safaris with champagne bush breakfast, guided walks with Maasai rangers in community areas bordering the reserve, Maasai village visits and cultural experiences, photography safaris with specialist guides, and day visits to the private conservancies (Naboisho, Mara North, Olare Motorogi) for night drives and off-road predator encounters form the core of the Masai Mara experience — with the Migration river crossing viewings at the Mara River from July to October representing the single most dramatic wildlife spectacle available anywhere in Africa.'
        }
      ],

      weatherPreview: {
        description: 'The Masai Mara sits at 1,500–2,000m with a temperate highland grassland climate. Temperatures range from 12°C to 28°C (54°F to 82°F) year-round. Two rainy seasons apply: long rains from March to May and short rains from October to November. The dry season from June to October coincides with the Wildebeest Migration making it peak season. January to March is an excellent second window.',
        linkText: 'More about the weather and climate'
      },

      bestTimePreview: {
        description: 'The Masai Mara is rewarding year-round. July to October is peak season, combining the Wildebeest Migration with the best wildlife density and dry-season conditions. January to March is an outstanding alternative with superb predator activity, beautiful green landscapes, and significantly fewer vehicles. Book 12 months ahead for July to September.',
        linkText: 'More about the best time to visit'
      },
