        title: 'Wildlife Highlights — Black Rhino, Lions & the City Skyline',
        description: `Nairobi National Park's black rhino population is its single most celebrated wildlife asset — one of the most important and reliably viewable black rhino concentrations in Kenya, made doubly remarkable by the backdrop of Africa's fourth-largest city. Multiple rhino individuals have well-documented home ranges and are encountered on the majority of morning game drives. Lion prides with well-established territories across the park's open grassland zones are encountered regularly year-round. Cheetah — both resident females with cubs and territorial males — are among the most reliably seen of Kenya's cheetah populations given the park's relatively open terrain. Leopard are present in the riverine forest along the Mbagathi and Athi River corridors but are secretive and less reliably encountered. From July to October, seasonal wildebeest and zebra migration from the Athi-Kapiti plains — entering through the park's unfenced southern boundary — brings large herds into the park and significantly increases predator activity. The combination of black rhino, lion, cheetah, and the Nairobi skyline creates one of the most distinctive and photographically unique wildlife environments in the world.`
