      gettingAround: `Ruma National Park is most practically reached by chartered aircraft from Nairobi Wilson Airport to Homa Bay Airstrip — a flight of approximately 60–75 minutes — followed by a 45-minute road transfer to the park gate. Overland from Nairobi via Kisumu takes approximately 7–8 hours (approximately 450km); the route passes through Kisumu and continues south to Homa Bay. A 4×4 is essential for the final approach and park tracks. Ruma can be combined with Lake Victoria (Homa Bay), Kakamega Forest (2 hours north), and Kisumu as part of a western Kenya circuit.`,
