          fullReview: 'I have birded across Kenya for fifteen years and visited Saiwa more times than I can count. It remains one of the most extraordinary small wildlife areas in all of East Africa. The Papyrus gonolek singing from the swamp edge at dawn is one of the most evocative bird sounds in Kenya. The sitatunga appearing from the papyrus into the open water as the mist lifts — always at roughly the same times, always at roughly the same places — feels like witnessing a private secret that the swamp has shared with you. The De Brazza\'s monkeys in the canopy above the boardwalk are among the most strikingly beautiful primates I have ever seen. And the bird list — 370-plus species in 3km² — is without equal in the density of its rewards per metre walked. Every visit to Saiwa reminds me why I became a field ornithologist.',
