          excerpt: 'Shaba gives you the northern five, the Ewaso leopards, and the volcanic landscape — without the vehicle clusters of a busy Samburu morning. For the serious wildlife traveller, it is the northern Kenya experience at its most essential.',
          fullReview: 'I have guided in the northern reserves for eighteen years. Shaba National Reserve is the experience I recommend to clients who have already visited Samburu, or who simply want the assurance of genuine exclusivity. The reserve has the same northern specials — Grevy\'s zebra, reticulated giraffe, Beisa oryx, gerenuk, Somali ostrich — that make Samburu famous. It has the same leopards along the Ewaso Nyiro, the same magnificent elephant bulls, the same extraordinary birdlife. But it receives a fraction of Samburu\'s visitors. On a busy July day in Samburu, a good leopard sighting can attract twelve or fifteen vehicles. In Shaba on the same day, you have the leopard to yourself, or nearly so. The volcanic scenery is genuinely unlike anything else in Kenya — the dark lava fields, the kopjes, the springs producing clear blue water in the middle of desert-like terrain. Shaba is not a lesser version of Samburu. It is its own extraordinary experience.',
