        fullReview: 'I came to Shaba because of Joy Adamson\'s book Queen of Shaba. I knew the story of her work with the leopard Penny in this reserve in the late 1970s and early 1980s, and I wanted to see the landscape she described. Shaba exceeded everything I expected. The volcanic scenery is extraordinary — dark lava flows, ancient kopjes scattered with doum palms, crystal springs producing blue-green water in the dry bush. We had a leopard on the second morning, sitting on an acacia above the lava field with a fresh kill. We had reticulated giraffe at the springs. Grevy\'s zebra. Oryx. And we had almost no other vehicles. Walking through this landscape knowing Adamson\'s story, watching a real leopard where she once watched Penny — there is no experience in Kenya that matches it for atmosphere and resonance. Extraordinary.',
