      gettingAround: `Shaba National Reserve is most practically reached by scheduled or chartered flight from Nairobi Wilson Airport to Samburu/Isiolo Airstrip (approximately 60–80 minutes), followed by a 30–45 minute road transfer east to the Shaba reserve boundary. Overland from Nairobi via Isiolo takes approximately 5–6 hours (350km) on the A2 highway. A capable 4×4 is essential inside the reserve. Shaba is most commonly combined with Samburu National Reserve and Buffalo Springs National Reserve as part of a multi-day northern Kenya experience.`,
      tourOperatorNote: 'We arrange fly-in logistics and combined Shaba-Samburu itineraries as part of our northern Kenya safari programmes.',
