      bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
        description: `Shimba Hills is excellent for birdwatching year-round. The coastal forest birds — Fischer's turaco, spotted ground thrush, Amani sunbird, African broadbill, and the East Coast akalat — are resident and viewable in all months, though the forest is most productive in the cool early morning hours. October to April brings Palearctic migrants and additional coastal waterbirds. For the most complete coastal Kenya forest bird list, combine Shimba Hills with Arabuko-Sokoke Forest near Watamu (3 hours north on the coast road) — together they represent the finest accessible coastal forest birdwatching in East Africa.`
      }
