          fullReview: 'I have worked with rhino across Kenya for twenty-five years — Lake Nakuru, Ol Pejeta, Meru, Nairobi, and numerous private conservancies. Solio Ranch is without parallel. The density of both species in a single property — approximately 190 rhino in 17,000 acres — means that a visit of two days is very unlikely to end without multiple encounters with both black and white rhino. But density alone does not explain what makes Solio exceptional. The mountain setting — the Laikipia grasslands with Mount Kenya filling the eastern sky — is one of the most beautiful landscapes in East Africa for wildlife photography. The walking safari, which brings guests to within metres of white rhino in open ground, is an experience of extraordinary privilege — the closest legitimate approach to wild rhino available anywhere in Africa. And the lodge itself, with its maximum ten guests, ensures that every sighting feels personal and unhurried. When clients ask me where to see rhino at their most magnificent, the answer is always Solio.',
