        description: `Solio is good for birdwatching year-round but is primarily visited for its rhino rather than its birds. The open grasslands are excellent for raptors — martial eagle, bateleur, secretary bird, and augur buzzard are all reliably encountered. The Solio River riverine forest holds African crowned eagle and a variety of forest species. October to April brings Palearctic migrants that dramatically increase the species list. For dedicated birders, combine Solio with the nearby Aberdare National Park or Mount Kenya forests for a more comprehensive Central Highlands bird circuit.`
