        description: `The Taita Hills endemic birds — Taita thrush, Taita apalis, and Taita white-eye — are resident year-round in the forest fragments (Ngangao, Chawia, Mbololo) above the sanctuary and are not significantly affected by season. An early start (gate by 5:30am, forest by 6:30am) is essential for the best encounters. A specialist local guide with knowledge of the specific forest sections where each endemic is most reliably found is strongly recommended — visiting the forests independently without local guidance significantly reduces the chance of finding these rare birds. Sanctuary savannah birdwatching is best from October to April when migrants arrive. For a complete southeastern Kenya bird circuit, combine Taita Hills with Tsavo East and Tsavo West.`
