      bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
        description: `Tsavo East is productive for birdwatching year-round. The Galana River is the most species-rich birdwatching corridor in the park, delivering African skimmer (one of East Africa's most sought-after riverine birds), Goliath heron, African fish eagle, carmine bee-eater colonies (August–October), and Nile crocodile at close range. The arid scrub delivers vulturine guineafowl, Somali bee-eater, rosy-patched bushshrike, and a wide range of raptors including martial eagle and bateleur. November to April brings Palearctic migrants that significantly expand the species list. Specialist birders should combine Tsavo East with Tsavo West and Taita Hills Wildlife Sanctuary for southeastern Kenya's complete bird list of over 600 species.`
      }
