          title: 'Tanzania\'s Most Underrated Park — Walking Safaris, Flamingos, and Mount Meru',
          rating: 5, visitedTimes: '400+ times',
          date: 'October 20, 2025',
          excerpt: 'Visitors arrive expecting a consolation prize. They leave understanding Arusha National Park is a completely different kind of experience — walking among giraffe, watching colobus in Ngurdoto forest, flamingo on the alkaline lakes.',
          fullReview: 'I have guided in Arusha National Park for eighteen years. In that time I have watched countless visitors arrive from the airport, spend one morning in the park before starting their Serengeti circuit, and leave surprised that this small park near the city has moved them as much as anything they encounter later. What Arusha National Park offers is not what the Serengeti offers. It offers intimacy — walking within fifteen metres of giraffe, sitting by the Momella Lakes as flamingos feed in the shallows, climbing through the colobus forest of Ngurdoto with no other group in sight. The absence of large predators means the animals are relaxed in a way that vehicle-only parks cannot replicate. The walking safari experience here is the finest in Tanzania\'s northern circuit, and it is still largely unknown to the mass market. Mount Meru is simply one of the finest mountain experiences in East Africa. I would not swap Arusha National Park for any park on the northern circuit.',
