          fullReview: 'We had one day between arriving at Kilimanjaro Airport and starting our Serengeti circuit. Our operator suggested Arusha National Park. I was sceptical — I had not heard much about it compared to the famous parks — and I was completely wrong to be. We drove to the Momella Lakes in the morning and watched hundreds of lesser flamingo feeding in the pink shallows with Kilimanjaro clear on the horizon behind them. We walked — actually walked, on foot, with our armed guide — among giraffe on the open plains. We visited the Ngurdoto Crater rim and watched colobus monkeys moving through the giant fig trees above us. In the afternoon, from the Momella area, we had both Mount Meru and Kilimanjaro simultaneously visible — a photographic composition I have never seen replicated. If you are doing a Tanzania northern circuit and have even one extra day, put it here.',
