        fullReview: 'This was my fourth Tanzania safari. I have been to the Serengeti three times, Ngorongoro twice, Tarangire twice. I added Arusha National Park on this trip because our operator recommended it and I had a free day. It was the single most memorable day of all four trips. We walked — on foot, not in a vehicle — and came within fifteen metres of a reticulated giraffe that watched us with calm curiosity for ten minutes before walking away. We canoed on the Momella Lakes among feeding flamingos and one large hippo that surfaced twelve metres from our canoe. We had the entire park to ourselves for most of the day. If this park were in Kenya\'s Masai Mara ecosystem it would be world-famous. Because it is near Arusha it is overlooked. Do not overlook it.',
