          fullReview: 'I have spent fifteen years at the Gombe Stream Research Centre studying the Kasekela community. I know individual chimpanzees — their names, their personalities, their family relationships, their histories of alliance and conflict — across three generations. When I guide visitors into the forest and we find Fudge, or Titan, or Gremlin\'s daughter, I can tell a story that no guide in any other park in Africa can tell — not because we are better guides, but because these particular chimpanzees have been known and studied for six decades. That continuity of knowledge — the depth of relationship between the research community and the chimpanzee community — is what makes Gombe unique on Earth. Every other primate tracking experience, however excellent, is a sighting. Gombe is an introduction.',
