          author: 'Patricia Horowitz',
          park: 'US', parkFlag: 'us',
          title: 'Sitting three metres from a chimpanzee with forty years of documented history — the finest wildlife hour of my life',
          rating: 5, date: 'September 5, 2025',
          excerpt: 'Our guide named every chimpanzee and told their life story. We sat three metres from an adult male who had been studied for forty years. He looked at us with intelligence. I will never forget Gombe.',
          fullReview: 'I have tracked gorillas in Rwanda and Uganda three times. I have been on safari across East and Southern Africa for twenty years. Nothing prepared me for Gombe. The forest is steep and beautiful. The lake below you is vast and clear and blue. And the chimpanzees — our guide, a researcher who has worked at Gombe for eleven years, introduced each individual by name and told us their family history and social relationships as we sat with them. We spent ninety minutes with a group of eight, including a mother with an infant. At one point an adult male sat within three metres of me, looked at me directly for perhaps thirty seconds, and went back to grooming. I have never looked into the eyes of a non-human animal and felt that quality of mutual recognition. Everything else I have done in wildlife travel — and I have done a great deal — is now divided into before Gombe and after Gombe.',
