          credentials: 'Singita senior field guide, 16 years Grumeti Reserve and western Serengeti, predator behaviour and migration ecology specialist.',
          title: 'The Private Serengeti — Grumeti River Crossings in Complete Solitude',
          rating: 5, visitedTimes: '600+ times',
          date: 'July 10, 2025',
          excerpt: 'In sixteen years at Grumeti, at the river crossings five kilometres inside our reserve, the only vehicles present have been ours. In the Serengeti National Park the same crossing would have forty vehicles. That is the difference Grumeti makes.',
          fullReview: 'I have guided in Grumeti for sixteen years. I have sat at the Grumeti River crossing and watched eight thousand wildebeest pile into the water while four of the largest Nile crocodile in the Serengeti ecosystem — animals that may be fifty or sixty years old — moved slowly and purposefully into position. And in sixteen years, at that specific crossing, the only vehicles present when the wildebeest committed to the river have been the vehicles I was driving. Not once have I sat at a Grumeti crossing with another operator\'s vehicle. This is the Singita model: exclusive traversing rights, strictly limited camp sizes, no concessions to volume. The Serengeti National Park is extraordinary. Grumeti is the Serengeti as it was before the safari industry discovered it — and it is available to those willing to invest in experiencing it that way.',
