        title: 'Best Time for Wildlife Viewing at Grumeti Game Reserve',
        description: `June and July are the peak months for the Grumeti River crossing — wildebeest columns move through the western corridor from late May and crossings can occur from early June to late July, though exact timing varies significantly between years. The permanent resident wildlife — lion, leopard, cheetah, elephant — makes Grumeti outstanding year-round. October to February is the best season for resident predator activity and the least-visited and most private period. The reserve is closed during the April to May heavy rain period when tracks become impassable.`
