          title: 'Four hundred hippos fighting in a shrinking pool, five hundred buffalo, and one vehicle — twenty years of safari and nothing compares',
          rating: 5, date: 'September 18, 2025',
          excerpt: 'Four hundred hippos, five hundred buffalo, the only vehicle in any direction. Twenty years of African safari and Katavi in September is the most powerful wildlife experience I have encountered.',
          fullReview: 'I have been going on safari in Africa for twenty years. Kenya, Tanzania, Botswana, Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Rwanda, Uganda. I have been to the Serengeti during the migration, to Ruaha in the dry season, to Moremi in the Okavango. I came to Katavi because a guide in the Selous told me I had not seen Africa until I had been there. He was right. On the first morning our guide Charles drove us to the Chada floodplain hippo pool at 7:00am. There were over four hundred hippos. The pool was perhaps one hundred metres in diameter. The fighting was continuous — not dramatic splashing but slow, grinding, horrible battles between enormous animals that left blood on the water and wounds on the bodies of the losers. We stayed for two and a half hours and no other vehicle appeared. In the afternoon a herd of what Charles estimated at five hundred buffalo moved across the plain in front of us. Lion — a pride of twelve — followed the herd openly on the plain, making no attempt to conceal their approach. We watched a hunt. No other vehicle was present at any point during the afternoon. In twenty years, those two game drives at Katavi in September are the most powerful wildlife experiences of my safari life. I am still attempting to process what I saw.',
