        rating: 5, date: 'August 30, 2025',
        excerpt: 'Three hours across the Chada Plain, not one other vehicle. The hippo pools. A pride of ten lion hunting buffalo at midday. Nothing in the northern circuit prepares you for Katavi.',
        fullReview: 'I have done the Tanzania northern circuit three times — Serengeti, Ngorongoro, Tarangire. I added Katavi to this trip because my operator said it would change my understanding of what safari means. They were correct. We drove across the Chada Plain for three hours on the first morning and did not see a single other vehicle. The hippo pool at the end of those three hours had perhaps three hundred animals in water that was barely enough to cover them. The fighting was constant and extraordinary. In the afternoon we found a pride of ten lion following a buffalo herd and watched them hunt for ninety minutes. At no point did another vehicle appear. This is the defining experience of Katavi: not just what you see, but that you see it completely alone. In the Serengeti the lion hunt would have had fifteen vehicles around it within minutes of the radio call. In Katavi there is no radio call. There is only you, your guide, and the Africa that still exists here.',
