      bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
        description: `Katavi's accessible season (July to October) coincides with excellent conditions for waterbird viewing — the shrinking Chada and Katisunga pools concentrate enormous numbers of open-bill stork, saddle-billed stork, wattled crane, African skimmer, and waterbirds of many species around the hippo pools and crocodile sandbanks of the Katuma River. Miombo specialists — Bohm's bee-eater, Stierling's woodpecker, racket-tailed roller, and pale-billed hornbill — are most active and vocal in July and August. Pel's fishing owl is regularly recorded along the Katuma River at dusk and dawn. Carmine bee-eater colonies are present along the Katuma riverbanks from August onwards. The vulture concentration around buffalo kills and hippo pool mortality events is extraordinary in September and October — up to five species of vulture can be seen simultaneously at a single carcass event.`
      }
