          'Flamingo and waterbird spectacle — in good years the alkaline lake holds hundreds of thousands of lesser and greater flamingo along with enormous concentrations of pelican, stork, and wading birds; this is one of East Africa\'s most visually spectacular natural events',
          'Outstanding groundwater forest — the giant fig and mahogany forest along the base of the escarpment is one of the most accessible tropical forest environments in Tanzania, with excellent elephant, baboon, blue monkey, and forest bird encounters',
          'Over 400 bird species — Lake Manyara is consistently listed among Tanzania\'s three finest birdwatching parks; the combination of lake, forest, and floodplain habitats delivers an extraordinary species diversity in a compact area',
