      latestUserReview: {
        id: 2, author: 'Pieter van der Berg', park: 'NL', parkFlag: 'nl',
        title: '127 bird species in eight hours — the finest birding day I have experienced in Africa',
        rating: 5, date: 'September 3, 2025',
        excerpt: '127 species in eight hours. Forest specialists, lake waterbirds, floodplain raptors. Lake Manyara is the finest single-day birding in Tanzania.',
        fullReview: 'I have been birdwatching in Africa for eighteen years. I have visited over thirty countries specifically for birds. Lake Manyara gave me 127 species in a single eight-hour day, which is one of the highest single-day counts I have ever achieved in East Africa outside of a specialist forest like Bwindi. The structure of the park is perfect for birding — the groundwater forest for forest specialists in the early morning, when the turacos and sunbirds and hornbills are most active and vocal; the lake shore for waterbirds, with flamingos and pelicans and saddle-billed stork and yellow-billed stork and spoonbill all in the same scan; the floodplain grassland for raptors and grassland birds. Our guide Grace knew every species and every location. The tree-canopy walkway adds additional forest birds that vehicle-based drives miss. Lake Manyara is consistently undervalued as a birding destination relative to the Serengeti and Ngorongoro. For pure species count and habitat diversity, it surpasses both.',
        helpful: 67, verified: true, tourTaken: 'Tanzania Birding Safari — Northern Circuit 10 Days', avatar: null
      }
