        fullReview: 'I have been on safari in Kenya, Tanzania (northern circuit), Uganda, Botswana, South Africa, and Zambia. I have seen the Big Five multiple times. I have done gorilla trekking in Uganda. Nothing has come close to the three hours I spent with the M-group at Mahale. The trek itself was demanding — steep, muddy, dense — but our guide James found the group within ninety minutes and we spent the rest of the time sitting on the forest floor while the chimpanzees moved around us. A young male approached to within arm\'s reach, looked directly at me, and moved on. The lake was visible through the trees behind the group. The forest was absolutely silent except for chimpanzee vocalisations. I have no vocabulary to adequately describe it. Mahale is in a category entirely separate from any other African wildlife experience I have had.',
