        title: 'Tanzania\'s Most Accessible Big-Game Safari — The Mkata Floodplain Delivers Northern Circuit Quality at a Budget Price',
        rating: 4, visitedTimes: '400+ times',
        date: 'September 18, 2025',
        excerpt: 'The Mkata floodplain in the morning with lion, elephant, giraffe, and zebra in open grassland is one of the finest and most underrated wildlife drives in Tanzania. Mikumi\'s reputation suffers from the highway — but get south of the road and the park is exceptional.',
        fullReview: 'Mikumi is Tanzania\'s most underrated national park. Its reputation suffers from two things: the highway through the north of the park, and the fact that it is not the Serengeti. Neither is a fair reason to undervalue it. The Mkata floodplain — south of the highway, early morning — delivers open-country game viewing comparable to the northern circuit. I have found four lion prides in a single morning on the floodplain. I regularly see herds of fifty or more elephant on the plains below the Uluguru Mountains backdrop. The giraffe and zebra are abundant and approachable. For anyone based in Dar es Salaam, or visiting Tanzania primarily for business with a free weekend, Mikumi offers a genuine and complete safari experience that no other park can match on accessibility and value.',
