      title: 'Mikumi surprised me completely — much better game than I expected',
      rating: 4, date: 'September 8, 2025',
      excerpt: 'The Mkata floodplain delivers genuine big-game viewing in an open landscape. Mikumi deserves far more credit.',
      fullReview: 'I had read that Mikumi was the poor cousin of Selous and that serious safari travellers should go straight to Nyerere. That assessment does Mikumi a disservice. The park\'s Mkata floodplain is genuinely impressive — a broad open plain with good game densities in an accessible landscape. The roads are well maintained. The accommodation at the main tented lodge was comfortable and very reasonably priced. We saw lion, elephant, buffalo, giraffe, zebra, and wildebeest in a single morning drive. The birding at the hippo pools was excellent. Is it the Serengeti? No. But for the access, the price, and the diversity of what you see, it is excellent value and a park I would return to.',
