    bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
      description: `Mikumi is excellent for birding year-round. The Miombo woodland specialists — Böhm's bee-eater, Stierling's woodpecker, Miombo rock thrush, racket-tailed roller — are resident and most active in the early morning from June to October. The Mkata floodplain delivers yellow-throated longclaw, wattled crane, saddle-billed stork, and goliath heron. November to April brings Palearctic migrants and the park's wetlands fill with breeding waterbirds. Mikumi is a particularly rewarding birding destination for visitors combining it with Nyerere (Selous) — the two parks share Miombo woodland endemics that are absent from the northern circuit.`
    }
