      description: `Ngorongoro Crater is excellent for birdwatching year-round. The open grassland delivers outstanding sightings of kori bustard, secretarybird, grey crowned crane, and raptors including bateleur, martial eagle, and augur buzzard. Lake Magadi is excellent for flamingo, pelican, and wading birds. The Lerai yellow-fever forest and the crater rim forest hold forest species. November to April brings Palearctic migrants including Montagu's harrier and European roller. The Tanzania endemic rufous-tailed weaver is reliably found on the crater floor. The rim forest holds Hartlaub's turaco, African crowned eagle, and highland forest species.`
