    factsAndFigures: { birdSpecies: '440+', migratoryBirds: 'Oct to Apr' },
    bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
      description: `Nyerere is outstanding for birding year-round when the park is open (June to March). The Rufiji River is excellent for African fish eagle, African skimmer, giant kingfisher, malachite kingfisher, saddle-billed stork, and the remarkable Pel's fishing owl in the riverine forest. The Miombo woodland delivers Böhm's bee-eater, Stierling's woodpecker, Miombo rock thrush, racket-tailed roller, and the suite of Miombo endemics absent from the northern circuit. The seasonal lakes are excellent for wading birds and waterfowl. October to April brings Palearctic migrants. Nyerere is the finest Miombo birding destination in Tanzania.`
    }
