      title: 'The Wami River at high tide — the finest boat safari I have taken in Tanzania',
      rating: 4, date: 'September 18, 2025',
      excerpt: 'Hippo at ten metres in the mangrove channel, crocodile everywhere, fish eagle overhead. The Wami River boat safari matched anything I have experienced on Tanzania\'s other rivers.',
      fullReview: 'I visited Saadani as a two-night add-on to Nyerere. I had done the Rufiji River at Nyerere and was told the Wami River at Saadani was comparable. That was a high bar. The Wami delivered — the boat safari on the incoming tide, with hippo at very close range in the mangrove channel, multiple Nile crocodile on the banks, African fish eagle calling from directly overhead, and the light in the mangroves at the end of the afternoon — was an extraordinary experience. The game drives at Saadani are not in the same league as Nyerere — the animal density is much lower and I would not choose Saadani as a standalone big-game destination. But as a coastal add-on with a world-class river boat safari, it added a genuinely different dimension to the Tanzania experience. And the beach is wonderful. Two nights at Saadani after Nyerere was a perfect Tanzania ending.',
