    factsAndFigures: { birdSpecies: '500+', migratoryBirds: 'Nov to Apr' },
    bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
      description: `Serengeti is outstanding for birding year-round. The open short-grass plains deliver kori bustard, secretary bird, grey crowned crane, and all the major grassland raptors. The Seronera valley riverine forest is exceptional for sunbirds, barbets, hornbills, and kingfishers. The open savannah provides lilac-breasted roller, superb starling, Fischer\'s lovebird, and the full suite of acacia-woodland species. The wetlands at Ndutu and along the Grumeti River hold yellow-billed stork, African fish eagle, saddle-billed stork, and waders. November to April brings Palearctic migrants including white stork, European roller, and a full suite of warblers and flycatchers. June to October offers the clearest viewing conditions and highest resident bird activity. The Serengeti\'s bird list is the largest of any Tanzania northern circuit park.`
    }
