      title: 'Wild dog denning season — sat with a pack of 24 every morning for three days',
      rating: 5, date: 'July 3, 2025',
      excerpt: 'Three mornings in a row at the den. Twenty-four adults and eleven pups. The most extraordinary predator encounter I have had in fifteen years of African safari travel.',
      fullReview: 'I planned this trip specifically for the wild dog denning season, following a tip from a guide at Nyerere who told me that Ruaha in June and July offered the most reliable wild dog denning in Tanzania. He was completely right. We found the den on the afternoon of day one — a pack of twenty-four adults with eleven pups. We returned every morning for the remaining three days of our stay and spent between two and three hours each morning as the pack became active and the pups emerged. The level of wild dog access was unlike anything I had experienced. No other vehicles. The guides maintained a respectful distance and the dogs ignored us completely. Beyond the wild dog, Ruaha delivered exceptional elephant — herds of thirty to fifty every morning along the river — a large lion pride with cubs, and a cheetah on the open plains on the last afternoon. The baobab landscape in the early morning light is extraordinarily beautiful. I will return to Ruaha every year for wild dog season.',
