    bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
      description: `Ruaha is exceptional for birding throughout the year. The Miombo woodland holds a suite of specials including Ruaha red-billed hornbill (near-endemic), Dickinson\'s kestrel, Stierling\'s woodpecker, Böhm\'s spinetail, Lilian\'s lovebird, and Souza\'s shrike — species unavailable at the northern circuit parks. The Great Ruaha River delivers African skimmer, Pel\'s fishing owl, giant kingfisher, African fish eagle, and African openbill. November to April brings Palearctic migrants. The dry season (June to October) offers the clearest viewing conditions. Ruaha\'s bird list, and particularly its Miombo woodland assemblage, makes it a priority destination for Tanzania birders seeking to add species unavailable elsewhere in East Africa.`
    }
