    bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
      description: `Bigodi is outstanding for birding year-round. The papyrus swamp is the most accessible location in Uganda for Papyrus Gonolek and Papyrus Yellow Warbler; both are resident and reliably encountered. The forest edge canopy delivers Great Blue Turaco, Black-and-white Casqued Hornbill, Bar-tailed Trogon, and Crowned Eagle. The forest floor and understorey hold African Pitta (most reliably November to April), White-tailed Ant Thrush, and White-spotted Flufftail. June to August and December to February offer the clearest path conditions and most active bird display. The Bigodi walk is an essential inclusion on any Uganda birding itinerary and adds species unavailable in Bwindi or Queen Elizabeth.`
    }
