      description: `Budongo is the finest lowland forest birding destination in Uganda. The Royal Mile — a straight path through ancient mahogany — is widely considered the best single birding walk in the country, delivering 60–80 species in a typical three-hour morning walk. Key species include Chocolate-backed Kingfisher (reliable at stream crossings), Ituri Batis (resident in the mid-storey fig section), Puvel\'s Illadopsis (heard and sometimes seen in the understorey), Nahan\'s Francolin (heard regularly; occasional views), and Cassin\'s Spinetail (canopy). The forest canopy delivers Crowned Eagle, Black-and-white Casqued Hornbill, Blue-throated Roller, and Red-sided Broadbill. June to August and December to February are the best months for the Royal Mile walk. The forest is birding year-round. Budongo adds Albertine Rift lowland species unavailable at the higher-altitude Bwindi.`
