      description: `Kibale National Park's defining wildlife feature is the habituated chimpanzee communities at Kanyanchu — the finest chimpanzee trekking experience on earth. Communities of 100–120 fully habituated individuals in undisturbed tropical forest, guided by trackers who know each individual by name and can interpret behaviour and social dynamics in real time, provide a wildlife encounter that consistently leaves visitors describing it as transformative. The park's second extraordinary feature is red colobus: 9,000 individuals in a single park — the largest population of any colobus species anywhere in Africa — visible in large groups at almost any point in the forest. Twelve additional primate species complete an assemblage that makes Kibale the most primate-rich forest on the planet. The Bigodi Wetland Sanctuary immediately adjacent to the park adds papyrus and wetland birding, more primates, and community-based tourism to an already outstanding destination.`
