    factsAndFigures: { birdSpecies: '475+', migratoryBirds: 'Nov to Apr' },
    bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
      description: `Kidepo Valley National Park has the highest bird species count of any Uganda national park — 475 species in an arid-zone savannah, rocky escarpment, and riverine forest ecosystem unique in Uganda. The Karamoja apalis — a range-restricted endemic found only in the Karamoja region — is reliably seen in the thicket vegetation near Apoka Lodge. The secretary bird and ostrich are seen on most morning game drives. The escarpments above the Narus Valley support Verreaux's eagle, martial eagle, and lappet-faced vulture. The wet season (April to May, October to November) brings migrants and the highest daily species counts. The dry season produces the clearest savannah conditions and the most accessible game-drive routes. Serious birders should allocate at least three full days to Kidepo and combine morning bird walks with afternoon and evening game drives.`
    }
