    highlights: {
      title: 'Wildlife Highlights — Uganda\'s Only Zebra, Horseback Safaris, Night Drives, and Boat Trips on Five Lakes',
      description: `Lake Mburo National Park's wildlife is defined by two uniquely Ugandan features — it is the only Uganda national park where zebra and impala are present — and by an exceptional diversity of activities that set it apart from any other Uganda park. The horseback safari (riding through acacia savannah in the presence of zebra, warthog, and buffalo, at distances only possible from horseback) is considered by most visitors the finest equestrian wildlife experience in East Africa. Night game drives produce leopard, serval, genet, African civet, and bush baby with greater reliability than any other Uganda park. Boat trips on Lake Mburo allow very close approaches to hippo and crocodile, with outstanding lakeside birding as a bonus. Twelve antelope species in 370km² makes the park one of the most antelope-rich in Uganda.`
    },
