      description: `Queen Elizabeth National Park is Uganda's second-finest birding park with 612 species across spectacularly diverse habitats. The Kazinga Channel boat cruise is the premier activity — shoebill stork, African skimmer, goliath heron, pink-backed pelican, pied and malachite kingfishers, and dozens of egret, heron, and ibis species are seen on virtually every cruise. Maramagambo Forest adds Albertine Rift endemics including Rwenzori batis and white-tailed lark. The Kyambura Gorge birding walk (separately from the chimp trek) adds forest species. Birding is good year-round; October to April brings Palearctic migrants and the highest waterbird concentrations.`
